{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For etc.</b> This verse corresponds to 'your heart meditates terror' (Isaiah 33:18), and there is none who judges anymore who says, 'So-and-so shall pay this tribute,' and the lawgiver is the scribe who writes who and who shall go to the king with tribute — for HaShem alone is our judge and our lawgiver and our king:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:34.646125156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}